      "writtenOn": "2023-12-19T14:29:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The way to think about the scaler context bits is that they are the storage area for your \"subclass\" of `SkGlyph`. We don\u0027t want a bunch of subclasses of `SkGlyph` because that gets messy fast and we want them all to be the same size for storage reasons. However, each logical subclass of `SkGlyph` does need somewhere to put some state, mostly to cache scaler context specific information computed in `generateMetrics` to later calls (at the moment this is mostly \"what format did I settle on?\").\n\nAs a result, feel free to use this bits however makes sense. At the moment you\u0027re kinda using the \"please create from path\" bit to get the metics from path, but you\u0027ll probably want to have an enum value for that and call `GenerateImageFromPath`.",
      "revId": "e21eda9c7aa7254421888d1ed3175863665d317b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
